  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 206 AM CST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nThe colder air behind the cold front will infiltrate into \nthe High Plains through the weekend into early next week. Saturday \nnight we will see a return to seasonable low temperatures dropping \ninto the upper teens to low 20s. Cooler with below normal high \ntemperatures will continue through mid-week. \n\nModels are suggesting another disturbance moves in early next \nweek. Latest model runs have showed inconsistencies with both \ntiming, currently one brining in the system very early Tuesday \nand one bringing it in late Tuesday. The track is a little \nfurther north in one model as opposed to another. The one thing \nthey can both agree on is the fact they both bring the system \nthrough as an open wave system. Will definitely need to monitor \nthis system as cooler, below normal high temperatures only in \nthe mid to upper 30s are expected mid-week, so any that does \noccur will likely be a rain/snow mix to all snow, potentially \nbringing the first snow of the season. The strength and track of\nthe system will keep evolving as models get a better handle on \nit once it moves onshore, but again something that will need to \nbe closely monitored, especially with the upcoming holiday.",
